# Chinese / UTF-8 (index.html)

Cursor `StrReplace` / `Write` on Windows has repeatedly turned CJK in `index.html` into `?`. This is a known project failure mode.

## Forbidden

- Do not use `StrReplace`, `Write`, or editor search-replace on `index.html` if the file contains Chinese (it always does).
- Do not run greedy regex like `main.js?v=[^"]+` against `index.html` (it can eat the file tail).
- Do not re-encode the file through PowerShell `Out-File`.

## Required

- Restore UI Chinese with `python scripts/restore_index_from_git.py` (rebuilds from `HEAD` + HUD extras).
- Cache-bump with `python scripts/bump_cache.py 29v` (ASCII query only, UTF-8 round-trip).
- After any `index.html` change, run `python scripts/assert_cjk.py` and fix before continuing.
- Other JS files with Chinese: prefer Python UTF-8 `Path.write_text(..., encoding="utf-8")` over `StrReplace` when the hunk includes CJK.

## Check

`index.html` must have hundreds of CJK code points and a Chinese `<title>` (浮骸). If the title is `??`, restore immediately — do not keep editing.
